# The turn rate of each stick's X at full and at half tilt, Harry standing still: the stick held for 2.5 s and watched
# from 0.5 s in until 0.5 s before its release, whatever the frame rate. The level is any but Entry where Harry is free
# from the start: GreatHall_G of the prototype, Grounds_hub of the retail game. rate.py's "view" is the camera's yaw
# (the player's view target), the rotation the sticks drive, and its "yaw" Harry's, which follows the camera.
#   tools/dev/inputtest/run.sh <run-tree> turn.scen <out-dir> GreatHall_G -NULLRENDERER
#   tools/dev/inputtest/rate.py <out-dir>/game.log 0
# The tags name the stick and the tilt (look-0.5: the look stick's X at half tilt); key-right is the Right arrow key.
waitlog Bringing Level (Entry[A-Za-z0-9_]|[A-DF-Za-z0-9_])[A-Za-z0-9_]*\.MyLevel up for play
sleep 15
pad attach
sleep 1
pad axis rightx 32767
sleep 0.5
watch 100000 look-1.0
sleep 1.5
watch 0 -
sleep 0.5
pad axis rightx 0
sleep 1
pad axis rightx 16384
sleep 0.5
watch 100000 look-0.5
sleep 1.5
watch 0 -
sleep 0.5
pad axis rightx 0
sleep 1
pad axis leftx 32767
sleep 0.5
watch 100000 move-1.0
sleep 1.5
watch 0 -
sleep 0.5
pad axis leftx 0
sleep 1
pad axis leftx 16384
sleep 0.5
watch 100000 move-0.5
sleep 1.5
watch 0 -
sleep 0.5
pad axis leftx 0
sleep 1
key Right 1
sleep 0.5
watch 100000 key-right
sleep 1.5
watch 0 -
sleep 0.5
key Right 0
sleep 1
